rm{Mn}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1b8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1b9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["60d3035daf049203d853666b"], "question": {"text": "The dark purple colour of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> disappears in the titration with oxalic acid in acidic medium. The overall change in the oxidation number of manganese in the reaction is"}, "options": [{"id": "f91ff3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1ba"}, {"id": "2b4e62", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1bb"}, {"id": "099dd7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1bc"}, {"id": "f8f860", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1bd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1be", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474b"], "question": {"text": "Mischmetal is an alloy consisting mainly of :"}, "options": [{"id": "1122f2", "text": "Lanthanoid metals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1bf"}, {"id": "66ad20", "text": "actinoid and transition metals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c0"}, {"id": "1d9aa7", "text": "lanthanoid and actinoid metals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c1"}, {"id": "0b3d33", "text": "actinoid metals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["6117b96e67dbe2603c3e9e62"], "question": {"text": "<p>The set of correct statements is:</p><p>(i)&nbsp;Manganese exhibits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math> oxidation state in its oxide.</p><p>(ii)&nbsp;Ruthenium and Osmium exhibit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math> oxidation in their oxides.</p><p>(iii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sc</mi></math> shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> oxidation state which is oxidizing in nature.</p><p>(iv)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> shows oxidising nature in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math> oxidation state.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ecf008", "text": "(ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c4"}, {"id": "2ee7d9", "text": "(i), (ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c5"}, {"id": "cfe48a", "text": "(i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c6"}, {"id": "f4fae1", "text": "(ii), (iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4742"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following acts as a strong reducing agent? (Atomic number : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ce</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>58</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Eu</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Gd</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Lu</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>71</mn><mo>)</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "5507e7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Lu</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1c9"}, {"id": "f06eef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Gd</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1ca"}, {"id": "5ef392", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Eu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1cb"}, {"id": "83a1c1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1cc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1cd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b54"], "question": {"text": "Thermal decomposition of a Mn compound <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> at <math><mn>513</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> results in compound <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and a gaseous product. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> reacts with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> and concentrated <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> to give a pungent gas