iant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d0"}, {"id": "a674e7", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95dc"], "question": {"text": "In which of the following pairs, the outermost&nbsp;electronic configuration will be the same?"}, "options": [{"id": "2e58ba", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mtext>and&#160;</mtext><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d3"}, {"id": "ebe8c9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d4"}, {"id": "e48048", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext><msup><mi>Co</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d5"}, {"id": "8f1c53", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "Diamagnetic Lanthanoid ions are:"}, "options": [{"id": "99abff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Nd</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Eu</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d8"}, {"id": "f6f272", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>La</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1d9"}, {"id": "8a41c9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Nd</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1da"}, {"id": "432fbe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Lu</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Eu</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1db"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1dc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["617aaa05ef3fe65ad8e851cb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I : Aqueous solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> is preferred as a primary standard in volumetric analysis over <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> aqueous solution.</p><p>Statement II : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> has a higher solubility in water than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>. In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7b1e64", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1dd"}, {"id": "9f3943", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1de"}, {"id": "773f39", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1df"}, {"id": "997c82", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["6162fbe46ed13040ec8543c9"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;with List<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math></p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;(process)</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math> (catalyst)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(a)</td>\t\t\t<td>Deacon&#39;s&nbsp;process</td>\t\t\t<td>(i)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZSM</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(b)</td>\t\t\t<td>Contact process</td>\t\t\t<td>(ii)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(c)</td>\t\t\t<td>Cracking of hydrocarbons</td>\t\t\t<td>(iii)</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(d)</td>\t\t\t<td>Hydrogenation of vegetable oils</td>\t\t\t<td>(iv)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below-</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "77e4d2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iii</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e2"}, {"id": "6f8528", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iv</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e3"}, {"id": "156fab", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ii</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e4"}, {"id": "1667a2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>iii</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1a2ee0e063d923a1e6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d